<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vaps Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1929–1934</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Estonian War of Independence Veterans' League</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vaps Movement, formally the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonian-war-of-independence">Estonian War of Independence</a> Veterans' League, was a radical right-wing populist movement of the early 1930s. It campaigned against parliamentary government and drafted the constitution approved by referendum in 1933, which created a powerful head of state. To prevent its victory in the coming elections, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-pats">Konstantin Päts</a> declared a state of emergency in March 1934 and banned it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vaps-movement.jpg" alt="Vaps Movement" width="320" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Finno-Ugric Man · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vapsid_logo.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
